{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-dimension","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0069","math_ordinal":193,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Section 211M defines Lebesgue measure on R^r.  The completeness test must therefore take an arbitrary subset B of that same ambient space; R is valid only in the special case r=1.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt211.tex:249","source_normalized_sha256":"282a1dd4cf4b21034d7086d7605ea16151d7bb70722ed7c0ead3ccde983c1b22","source_text":"$B\\subseteq\\Bbb R$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt211.tex:267","target_normalized_sha256":"5f3106e1ddbecda96e88d235a978b68760b104483a734daece907b4bb0997529","target_text":"$B\\subseteq\\BbbR^r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S211"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-positive-measure-hypothesis","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0070","math_ordinal":207,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof immediately uses lim f(n)=mu E>0 and the intermediate value theorem to find a subset of measure strictly between 0 and mu E.  That conclusion requires E to have positive measure.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt211.tex:266","source_normalized_sha256":"afe4bbaaedba5158924d3a0bd77f0304472650e71de5aed22515cc3a0a8e1bd2","source_text":"$E\\in\\Sigma$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt211.tex:285","target_normalized_sha256":"0a52244951b5859f7d5c463794b9d25f2de3dd97a545734588d6644dcb00eccd","target_text":"$E\\in\\Sigma,\\ \\mu E>0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S211"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-quantifier-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0071","math_ordinal":462,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The least-upper-bound condition in 211Ya must quantify over members of the selected subfamily A.  Quantifying over every member of the whole measure algebra would demand a top element rather than the supremum of A.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt211.tex:511","source_normalized_sha256":"b538a05fd20d55430c234fcba4e12ff08942be0ea2947040cfc1c9a155d66366","source_text":"$a\\in\\frak A$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt211.tex:563","target_normalized_sha256":"1e105b215fd2d4e7c99395aa9447b20db49916f38921e66c942de0ab5c834282","target_text":"$a\\in A$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S211"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-quantifier-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0072","math_ordinal":481,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The countable-supremum condition in 211Yb must quantify over members of the given countable subfamily A, exactly as in 211Ya, not over every member of the measure algebra.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt211.tex:526","source_normalized_sha256":"b538a05fd20d55430c234fcba4e12ff08942be0ea2947040cfc1c9a155d66366","source_text":"$a\\in\\frak A$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt211.tex:580","target_normalized_sha256":"1e105b215fd2d4e7c99395aa9447b20db49916f38921e66c942de0ab5c834282","target_text":"$a\\in A$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S211"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-order-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0073","math_ordinal":482,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The objects h and g are equivalence classes in the measure algebra, ordered by the relation Bsubseteq introduced in 211Ya; ordinary set inclusion is not the defined order on these objects.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt211.tex:526","source_normalized_sha256":"0b31539bcb64bc14349cc7f749a590c104b9b0a930fbc497739f60e84c70b8f0","source_text":"$h\\subseteq g$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt211.tex:580","target_normalized_sha256":"ed942be50bd9d288bf34398559489502e6076cf05261595dce32dd1ce7e7b14d","target_text":"$h\\Bsubseteq g$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S211"}
